Article 12
Regional Government encourages community participation as referred to in Article 6 letter e, by means of:
a. fostering community awareness towards cases of acts of violence against women and children;
b. encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting acts of violence against women and children;
c. fostering local wisdom in handling cases of acts of violence;
d. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling acts of violence against women and children;
e. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to acts of violence against women and children.

Article 7
- 7 - (1) Regional Government conducts prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter a through empowerment and awareness to Families, Parents, and the Community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), it shall be implemented by means of:
a. providing material on prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern towards prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and
g. opening an integrated service system for protection of women and children from acts of violence in every kelurahan.

Article 8
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 7, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population administration and civil registration;
f. women's empowerment, protection of women and children; g. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises; and
h. public tranquility, public order, and community protection (2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 18
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is prompt, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and - 11 -
j. the right to a sense of security and protection.

