Article 9
Regional Government conducts legal protection as referred to in Article 6 letter b, covering:
a. providing protection in Safe Houses;
b. providing legal information to victims;
c. providing assistance for victims as witnesses from the investigation process until the verdict; and - 8 -
d. providing special legal protection for child victims of acts of violence which can be carried out through the appointment of guardianship in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 2
The protection of women and children from acts of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. order and legal certainty;
e. transparency; and
f. protection.

Article 3
The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence, are to:
a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including human trafficking;
b. eliminate all forms of acts of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services to women and children from acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. empower women and children victims of acts of violence to be more empowered both physically, psychologically, socially, and economically.
